FUNDAMENTALS
Sets:     X  (domain / inputs)
          Y  (codomain / outputs)
Map:      f : X → Y
Pairs:    {(x, y) ∈ X × Y | y = f(x)}
Rule:     each x ∈ X has exactly one y ∈ Y

A function f from X to Y is the set of ordered pairs
{(x, y) ∈ X × Y | y = f(x)}
such that every x has precisely one image y.

NOTATION
f : X → Y
